  "question": {
    "text": "The probability of a problem being solved by <math><mn>3</mn></math> students independently are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> respectively. If the probability that the problem is solved is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>S</mi></mfenced></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>S</mi></mfenced></math> lies in the interval (where,&nbsp;<math><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>)"
  },
